{"skill":{"slug":"web-browsing","displayName":"Web Browsing"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1773452133128,"changelog":"Initial release of the web-browsing skill.\n\n- Enables browsing and summarizing websites, extracting content from URLs, and searching the web for information.\n- Provides tools for web search, direct URL content retrieval, and HTML content extraction.\n- Includes guidelines and best practices for effective use.\n- Outlines current limitations, including handling of dynamic sites and login-required pages.","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"references/usage-guide.md","size":1924,"sha256":"25f834dffb39816ddc78d863aae23ccc0ca64f172267e07c2b2e87f9e8ffe7ac","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/search_web.py","size":3409,"sha256":"1251fe5341f593884d7722f5ea0607db7e3047dcac9d9ba7aaec9af244545393","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2389,"sha256":"858cd88f6ac8e54af0c4151dd08776614e0d366ecf0ba6ed85afab0cf2797cf2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2059,"sha256":"4005544e39960457dcf65c0307d11c09770f75aa7f8db649491b1a2712630049","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789175241901,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a1d679d498cc2073f9712846e5385628d4ad3c3ef27a707dc42cb5e14679db6a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a1d679d498cc2073f9712846e5385628d4ad3c3ef27a707dc42cb5e14679db6a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086021003},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":27,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789175241901},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This web-browsing skill does what it says, but needs review because it can fetch any URL from the agent's network without safeguards.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access is proportionate for a browsing skill, but unrestricted outbound fetching from the agent runtime is under-scoped because it may reach localhost, private-network, link-local, metadata, or redirected destinations.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No install hooks, package-install commands, tool replacement, or automatic setup behavior were found; the artifact ships a markdown skill, a usage guide, and one helper script.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions clearly describe broad web search and URL-fetch behavior, but they do not define a permission boundary or warn users that queries and URLs are sent to external services and target sites.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence, credential access, session/profile use, privilege escalation, memory modification, scheduled task, or background worker behavior was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Searching the web and fetching pages are aligned with the stated web-browsing purpose, but fetch_url accepts arbitrary caller-provided URLs, follows redirects, and returns page content without destination validation.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with the agent sending your search terms and provided URLs to external services. Do not use it with secrets, private/internal URLs, credentials in query strings, or sensitive personal data unless the runtime has strong outbound network controls. The publisher should add URL validation, redirect revalidation, private-network blocking, download limits, and clear privacy disclosure before this is treated as low-risk.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Network-capable browsing is expected for this skill, but the artifact does not provide explicit tool scoping or a clear permission boundary, so this remains a governance concern rather than evidence of malicious intent.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending search terms to DuckDuckGo and URLs to target websites is inherent to the browsing purpose, but the user-facing documentation does not disclose that privacy impact or warn against secrets, internal URLs, or tokenized links.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The arbitrary URL fetcher with redirects and no scheme, host, IP, or destination-class validation creates an SSRF-style risk that is not necessary for safe web browsing.\n[T09] unexpected: The static SSRF finding is supported by artifact code: requests.get(url, allow_redirects=True) uses caller-controlled input and returns extracted content, making internal or redirected responses potentially visible to the caller.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789175241901}}}}}